      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXII.—खलेषु संसर्गमुक्तिः is an instance of the so-called एकदेशी",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "अन्वय like देवदत्तस्य गुरुकुलम्. खलेषु यः संसर्गस्तस्मान्मुक्तिः. This Stanza",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "occurs also in the Kâvyasangraha p. 4 and in the Mahânâṭaka p.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "38 (Calc. Ed. 1870).—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXIII.—वाक्पटुता = पक्षपातराहित्येन वादित्वम् says Râmarshi but it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "simply means cleverness in speaking. Râmarshi's idea is not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "necessarily involved in the word.—Drutavilambita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXIV.—संभ्रमविधिः = आदरविधिः according to the commentary.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Bohlen I observe, quotes the authority of the Vis'vakosha for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "this; संभ्रमः साध्वसेपि स्यात्संवेगादरयोरपि. The usual meaning of hurry may",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "also do. It would mean the flutter of preparation to do due honour.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "See Amara I. Nâṭyavarga 34 and commentary (हर्षादिना कर्मसु त्वरणम्)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "and compare Vikramorvashî संभ्रमादरगर्भम्. विधि means simply doing,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "performing. Comp. Gangâlaharî St. 38 among many other in-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "stances. उपकृति, in the reading adopted in the text, must mean fa-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "vours received. अनुत्सेक freedom from pride comp. S'âkuntala भाग्ये-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "ष्वनुत्सेकिनी—निरभिभवसार = not full of disrespect (i. e. expressions of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "disrespect or condemnation) Comp. Mâgha XVI., 29 et seq. —",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXV.—कर. Some copies of the commentary render this by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "कृत्य, wrongly, and without authority. कर means hand here as is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "clear from the context.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXVI.—महाशैलशिलासंघात = collection of the stones of a big",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "mountain.—Anushṭub.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXVII.—स्वात्याम् = (See Varâhamihira chap. XV., 13) स्वातीसंज्ञ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "नक्षत्रे सूर्ये स्थिते सति (commentary). Comp. Mâlavikâgnimitra p. 7.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "(Bombay Sans. Class.).—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r9",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXVIII.—एव is better construed with हितम् than with भर्तुः.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Râmarshi says पत्युरेव हितमिच्छति but adds न रूपादिमदि( त्त्वमि ?) त्यर्थः.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
